###Observations of inter-pack conflict and instability in contiguous dingo packs.###

#Code and data used to generate observations of dingo pack behaviours during the deaths of dominant individuals. 
#Data presented here was collected to as part of research projects studying a population of dingoes in the Myall Lakes region of NSW, Australia. 
#Data from the paper consist of three sources: 
#1) camera trap data photos from cameras placed on trails, designed to estimate dingo population density in the area using spatial capture recapture;
#2) Camera trap videos recording dingo scent marking behaviour; 
#3) On-ground observations from local land managers. Here the first two data sources are supplied

#Follow scripts in order. 

Published paper link : DOI:10.1002/ece3.74376
